1
00:00:01,010 --> 00:00:03,130
Hello everyone and welcome to EnglishPod.

2
00:00:03,370 --> 00:00:03,810
My name is Marco.

3
00:00:04,190 --> 00:00:06,870
My name is Kathryn and we're going to the gym today, right Marco?

4
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:07,570
That's right.

5
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:13,410
Today we're going to go to the gym and we're going to try to lose weight or to get in shape.

6
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:18,850
So before we start out though, there is a phrasal verb that we should take a look at.

7
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:23,850
So today in Vocabulary Preview, we're looking at this phrase, to work out or working out.

8
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:24,800
That's right.

9
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:26,960
So when we go to the gym, this is what we do.

10
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:32,480
We go there to work out, to exercise or to tone up.

11
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:38,460
This is just a way of saying that I'm going to go somewhere like a gym to exercise myself.

12
00:00:38,820 --> 00:00:39,320
That's right.

13
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:47,720
So with that in mind, we're going to go to the gym, we're going to work out and we're going to learn a lot of words today about what exactly goes on in the gym.

14
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:55,080
Do you want to go catch a movie tonight?

15
00:00:55,660 --> 00:00:56,140
I can't.

16
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:56,940
I have to go to the gym.

17
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:58,640
Come on.

18
00:00:58,640 --> 00:00:59,640
You can go tomorrow.

19
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:00,640
Just skip it today.

20
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:01,240
It's not as if you're going to get in trouble.

21
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:02,800
Actually, I will.

22
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:06,000
I'm working out with a personal trainer that gets on my case if I don't go.

23
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:09,620
I like it because it makes me feel more obligated to go and get healthy.

24
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:10,580
That's cool.

25
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:13,040
Does your personal trainer basically teach you how to work out?

26
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:13,720
Yeah.

27
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:18,720
He makes a workout plan depending on the areas I want to work on or the muscles I want to build.

28
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:25,240
Like for example, in order to get better muscle tone in my abs, pecs and biceps, he makes me work out with free weights.

29
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:28,130
Then for my quads, calves and hamstrings, I do leg lifts or squats.

30
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:30,590
Sounds like you're really getting into shape.

31
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:33,520
All right.

32
00:01:34,630 --> 00:01:35,430
So, now we're back.

33
00:01:35,630 --> 00:01:37,150
Let's take a look at Language Takeaway.

34
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:40,840
Language Takeaway.

35
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:43,120
All right.

36
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:47,680
First of all, in today's dialogue, we heard a lot about this person called a personal trainer.

37
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:49,880
What does a personal trainer do, Marco?

38
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:59,290
So basically, you have a person that is your coach, the person that guides you and teaches you how to work out or what you should do.

39
00:01:59,770 --> 00:01:59,990
All right.

40
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:02,090
So, personal means it's just for me.

41
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:03,750
This person is only helping me.

42
00:02:04,410 --> 00:02:07,490
A trainer is someone who, like you say, gives me guidance.

43
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:17,200
So personal trainer is someone who will work with me every day or maybe one time a week to really get the most out of my workout.

44
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:17,370
That's right.

45
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:19,330
So that is a personal trainer.

46
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:23,490
And as we said, he's going to help us to build muscle.

47
00:02:24,090 --> 00:02:25,630
We want to build muscle when we go to the gym.

48
00:02:25,850 --> 00:02:26,030
All right.

49
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:30,570
So, this is an interesting one because the verb is not to grow or to make.

50
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,350
The verb is to build.

51
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:36,390
So, I have muscles, but I want my muscles to get bigger.

52
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:38,770
So I go to build muscles at the gym.

53
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:42,880
You might even hear this phrase, a bodybuilder.

54
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:44,190
So this idea that you make them.

55
00:02:44,730 --> 00:02:45,450
Yeah, exactly.

56
00:02:45,770 --> 00:02:47,580
So you don't get muscle.

57
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:49,000
You don't create muscle.

58
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:50,160
You build muscle.

59
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:55,560
And alongside with muscles, not only do you get them big, but you also get muscle tone.

60
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:56,800
All right.

61
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:59,520
So muscle tone basically means definition.

62
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:06,200
So maybe before you start to work out, your body is very soft.

63
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:07,140
You can't see the muscles.

64
00:03:07,740 --> 00:03:10,820
Well, when you start to see those muscles, you see the lines in your body.

65
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:12,980
Your skin gets tighter, not so soft.

66
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:14,280
That's called muscle tone.

67
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:15,080
That's right.

68
00:03:15,180 --> 00:03:16,840
So then you can see the muscles.

69
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:17,720
That's muscle tone.

70
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:24,240
And now the muscles that we most commonly go to the gym to work out, we're going to name really quickly and we're going to see where they are.

71
00:03:24,420 --> 00:03:26,560
So the first one that we mentioned were abs.

72
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:27,400
Okay.

73
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:29,780
This is an important one, especially if you want to go to the beach.

74
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:33,080
The abs are located on your stomach.

75
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:37,480
So you see those kind of rectangles, those squares on your stomach.

76
00:03:38,460 --> 00:03:39,380
Those are the abs.

77
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:40,140
That's right.

78
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:45,080
And now for guys also, we want to work out our pecs or our pectoral muscles.

79
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:50,860
So those are on your chest, below your neck, but above your stomach.

80
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:51,660
That's right.

81
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:55,400
And another important one on your arm, we have our biceps.

82
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:56,440
All right.

83
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:59,100
Men usually like to show these off, or at least boys do.

84
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:00,820
These are on your arms.

85
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:04,940
So you know when you make that L shape with your arm and you squeeze like Popeye?

86
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:06,920
Those are your biceps.

87
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:08,000
Those are your biceps.

88
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:08,520
Exactly.

89
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:14,760
And now, obviously going down towards our legs now, we have our quad muscles, our quads.

90
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:15,760
All right.

91
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:17,420
So those are on the top part of your legs, right Marco?

92
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:19,120
In front.

93
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:20,120
In front.

94
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:20,760
So like on the top of your thigh.

95
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:22,560
Exactly.

96
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:29,300
And now right behind the back part of your leg, you have your hamstrings.

97
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:30,720
Hamstring.

98
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:37,240
Now you hear about this one a lot because people injure their hamstrings pretty easily in football or in running.

99
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:38,140
Yeah, that's right.

100
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:43,560
Sometimes if you're running and you didn't stretch, your muscles are not warm, you can pull a hamstring.

101
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:44,340
All right.

102
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:45,900
So that hamstring is an important one.

103
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:46,620
We have one more.

104
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:47,500
That's right.

105
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:50,620
We have our calves and these are in the bottom, right above our feet.

106
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:54,340
So I don't have any muscles except for this one because I ride my bike.

107
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:56,000
And when you ride your bike, this gets big.

108
00:04:56,180 --> 00:05:01,500
So your calves are that part of your leg above your foot, but below your knee in the back.

109
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:02,160
That's right.

110
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:02,980
The back part.

111
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:04,920
Very good.

112
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:08,180
So all of these muscles, some of the most common ones that we work out.

113
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:13,140
So now let's move on to some important phrases on Fluency Builder.

114
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:20,550
Do you want to go catch a movie tonight?

115
00:05:21,170 --> 00:05:21,630
I can't.

116
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:22,430
I have to go to the gym.

117
00:05:22,810 --> 00:05:23,190
Come on.

118
00:05:23,490 --> 00:05:23,990
You can go tomorrow.

119
00:05:24,230 --> 00:05:24,950
Just skip it today.

120
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:26,710
It's not as if you're going to get in trouble.

121
00:05:27,270 --> 00:05:28,290
Actually, I will.

122
00:05:28,650 --> 00:05:31,490
I'm working out with a personal trainer that gets on my case if I don't go.

123
00:05:31,810 --> 00:05:35,110
I like it because it makes me feel more obligated to go and get healthy.

124
00:05:35,670 --> 00:05:36,050
That's cool.

125
00:05:36,410 --> 00:05:38,550
Does your personal trainer basically teach you how to work out?

126
00:05:38,850 --> 00:05:39,210
Yeah.

127
00:05:39,870 --> 00:05:44,190
He makes a workout plan depending on the areas I want to work on or the muscles I want to build.

128
00:05:44,550 --> 00:05:50,250
Like, for example, in order to get better muscle tone in my abs, pecs, and biceps, he makes me work out with free weights.

129
00:05:50,630 --> 00:05:53,610
Then for my quads, calves, and hamstrings, I do leg lifts or squats.

130
00:05:54,030 --> 00:05:56,070
Sounds like you're really getting into shape.

131
00:06:00,110 --> 00:06:03,450
So the beginning of the dialogue, the friends were trying to decide what to do.

132
00:06:03,750 --> 00:06:06,650
And one friend said, do you want to go catch a movie?

133
00:06:07,010 --> 00:06:07,450
That's right.

134
00:06:07,750 --> 00:06:09,290
So to catch a movie.

135
00:06:09,370 --> 00:06:10,370
Do you want to go catch a movie?

136
00:06:10,570 --> 00:06:15,330
It sounds funny because catch means to hold something in your hands after someone throws it.

137
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:17,320
So throw and catch.

138
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:21,310
But here, it doesn't mean to actually hold something in your hands.

139
00:06:21,670 --> 00:06:24,930
It means do you want to go see a movie?

140
00:06:25,050 --> 00:06:25,270
Right.

141
00:06:25,390 --> 00:06:25,790
Exactly.

142
00:06:26,450 --> 00:06:30,130
So it's a very informal, colloquial way of saying, hey, do you want to go to the movies?

143
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:32,220
Do you want to go see a movie?

144
00:06:32,220 --> 00:06:34,910
Maybe not like a serious date or something, just for fun.

145
00:06:35,230 --> 00:06:36,110
Do you want to go catch a movie?

146
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:36,790
That's right.

147
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:38,600
Let's go catch a movie.

148
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:39,600
All right.

149
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:41,960
So obviously we can't go to the movies because we got to go to the gym.

150
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:46,890
And we have to go to the gym because our personal trainer will get on our case.

151
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:50,270
The personal trainer will get on my case if I don't go.

152
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:51,520
All right.

153
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:55,240
So someone will get on my case if I don't do this.

154
00:06:56,480 --> 00:07:04,780
So this is an interesting way of saying, my personal trainer will criticize me or will be angry with me if I don't do this.

155
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:05,480
That's right.

156
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:08,080
So you can use it with, for example, your parents.

157
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:11,600
Your parents are always getting on your case because you don't clean your room.

158
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:12,610
Yeah.

159
00:07:12,610 --> 00:07:17,350
My mom gets on my case when I don't tell her where I'm going when I go out.

160
00:07:17,610 --> 00:07:23,850
So that means to criticize, to give you a hard time, to get angry at you or even maybe yell at you.

161
00:07:24,070 --> 00:07:25,730
But you can change the pronoun.

162
00:07:26,260 --> 00:07:30,620
So he gets on my case, but I can get on your case.

163
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:31,160
That's right.

164
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:35,760
So remember that someone gets on someone else's case.

165
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:37,020
That's where the person goes.

166
00:07:37,660 --> 00:07:42,720
And of course, if you want to tell that person to stop bothering you, you just say, get off my case.

167
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:43,000
All right.

168
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:44,300
So he's on her case.

169
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:45,880
Get off my case.

170
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:46,540
That's right.

171
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:52,780
And now to finish things off, the whole reason why we're going to the gym is because we want to get in shape.

172
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:53,600
All right.

173
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:55,360
Great phrase here to get in shape.

174
00:07:55,580 --> 00:07:58,220
This is something a lot of people like to do in the new year.

175
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:00,760
So they say, okay, it's a new year.

176
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:01,540
I want a new body.

177
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:03,480
I'm going to get in shape.

178
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:08,120
That means I will lose weight, build some muscle and start to feel good.

179
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:08,740
That's right.

180
00:08:08,820 --> 00:08:10,180
So we want to get in shape.

181
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:11,800
Very good.

182
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:13,440
Let's listen to our dialogue one last time.

183
00:08:19,840 --> 00:08:20,820
Do you want to go catch a movie tonight?

184
00:08:21,420 --> 00:08:21,880
I can't.

185
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:22,680
I have to go to the gym.

186
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:23,460
Come on.

187
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:24,280
You can go tomorrow.

188
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:25,180
Just skip it today.

189
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:26,980
It's not as if you're going to get in trouble.

190
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:28,540
Actually, I will.

191
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:31,740
I'm working out with a personal trainer that gets on my case if I don't go.

192
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:35,360
I like it because it makes me feel more obligated to go and get healthy.

193
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:36,320
That's cool.

194
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:38,800
Does your personal trainer basically teach you how to work out?

195
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:39,480
Yeah.

196
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:44,460
He makes a workout plan depending on the areas I want to work on or the muscles I want to build.

197
00:08:44,810 --> 00:08:50,530
Like for example, in order to get better muscle tone in my abs, pecs and biceps, he makes me work out with free weights.

198
00:08:50,890 --> 00:08:53,870
Then for my quads, calves and hamstrings, I do leg lifts or squats.

199
00:08:54,680 --> 00:09:01,080
Seems like you're really getting into shape.

200
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:03,720
Going to the gym, getting a personal trainer, what do you think?

201
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:05,200
Is it a good idea or a bad idea?

202
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:15,520
I think for some people who have a hard time getting motivated, so people who don't like to go to the gym, it's a great idea because having another person push you can really help.

203
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:21,180
I think for other people who are already pushing themselves, it's not as helpful.

204
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:38,960
I think also if you just start out going to the gym, I think you should get a personal trainer for the first couple of weeks because you really have to understand and learn what you're doing and the purpose of that exercise and figure out how many sets, how many repetitions.

205
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:43,140
This is very important because some people just go and they overwork it.

206
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:46,860
They do and they don't know how to use the machines or the weights.

207
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:48,660
You can actually harm yourself.

208
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:53,440
You can pull a hamstring or something if you don't know what you're doing.

209
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:58,260
For people who've never learned how to exercise, maybe it's a good idea like you say.

210
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:00,160
It's a very interesting thing.

211
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:04,940
Actually gyms as well, very popular nowadays, especially with the holidays passing.

212
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:07,180
People gain some holiday weight.

213
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:09,520
You got to go back to the gym to lose that weight.

214
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:10,520
That's right.

215
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:11,520
Let us know.

216
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:12,520
Do you go to the gym?

217
00:10:12,520 --> 00:10:14,970
If so, what parts of your body do you like to focus on?

218
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:16,600
Our website is EnglishPod.com.

219
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:17,600
All right.

220
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:17,930
We'll see you guys there.

221
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:19,600
Take care.

222
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:27,017
Bye bye.
